    title: 'Every count on an Audits row opens exactly what it counted',
    what: 'Every number on an Audits row is a question — <b>24 warning</b> is "which twenty-four?" — and until now the answer was several clicks away. <b>They are all buttons now.</b> Clicking <b>24 warning</b> opens that website showing exactly those twenty-four items, and the same goes for critical, outdated, info, for clarification and on hold. The counts use the same rule the audit list filters by, so the number you clicked and the list you land on always agree.<br><br>The <b>💬</b> count was the worst of them: a number with nowhere to go — and a confusing one, because it counts every comment on the website <b>including the ones left on individual audit items</b>, which the Discussion tab was hiding by default. So three comments could lead to a page showing none of them. Now it is a button: click it and the discussion opens with item comments included, scrolled to the newest, each one saying which item it belongs to. Going the other way, <b>Show the discussed audit items</b> filters the audit list to just the items being talked about — the same thing as the new <b>💬 Discussed</b> chip beside Critical and Warning.<br><br>And when a click somewhere else sets a filter for you, the app now <b>flashes the control that did it</b> for a couple of seconds, so the next time you know where to reach. A filtered audit list also says so above the table — <b>Showing 2 of 38 · filtered by …</b> — with a Clear filters link, whether or not the result is empty.',
